course: dictionary
lesson: 251
title: Alphabetical order
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Alphabetical means arranged in the order of the letters of the alphabet, from A to Z. Words are sorted this way in dictionaries, registers and library shelves.
explain: To sort words, look at the first letter. Apple comes before banana because a comes before b. If the first letters match, look at the second letter: cap comes before cat, because a comes before t at the third letter, and both words share c and a.
explain: The example sentence says, «"Facetious" (jokey at the wrong moment) has the vowels a, e, i, o, u once each, in alphabetical order.» Read the word letter by letter and you will see the vowels appear in the order a, e, i, o, u, which is the order of the alphabet.
fact: Alphabetical means arranged in the order of the letters of the alphabet, from A to Z.
fact: Alphabetical is an adjective, and alphabetically is an adverb: «The names are sorted alphabetically.»
fact: To sort words, compare the first letters; if they match, compare the second letters, and so on.
fact: Libraries sort fiction by the author's surname, alphabetically.
fact: «Facetious» has the vowels a, e, i, o, u, once each, in alphabetical order.
exercise: Put these words in alphabetical order: dog, cat, bird. Which word comes first? | *Cat | Dog | Bird
exercise: Which word comes first in alphabetical order? | Banana | Zebra | *Cherry | Apple
exercise: In «"Facetious" has the vowels a, e, i, o, u once each, in alphabetical order», which word means jokey at the wrong moment? | vowels | *Facetious | order | alphabetical
test: Which word comes first in alphabetical order: cap or cat? | *Cap | They are the same | Cat
test: What order are the vowels in «facetious»? | *a, e, i, o, u | u, o, i, e, a | e, a, u, o, i | i, a, o, e, u
exam: Sort these into alphabetical order: pencil, ruler, eraser. Which word is in the middle? | *Eraser | Ruler | None of them | Pencil
